{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>A tower of strength is the name of YHWH</b> [and] <b>the righteous runs into it</b> [Proverbs 18:10] — three joined elements." "<b>into it</b> — into His name he runs, so that he does not stumble, or he crushes his enemy, even though it is in the šoreq (the holem-vav vocalization), like: אָרוּץ גְּדוּד (I will run against a troop) [2 Samuel 22:30]; and he is exalted at the time He surrounds him, and [the enemy] cannot prevail against him."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {0 "The bracketed [י-יב] appears to be a manuscript notation; retained literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:23:31.004277091Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}